From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] unidrv: makers' PCL 6 drivers -- vector plug-ins, value macros in commands, PCL XL raster

HP's Universal Printing PCL 6 driver -- the driver of most office laser
printers -- is a GPD on Unidrv with a render plug-in that writes PCL XL
itself from the drawing calls it hooks. On our Unidrv its job was not PCL
XL a printer could read:

- The plug-in's devmode part was asked for without the driver object, so
  the plug-in (which asks the core about the printer then) refused, and
  its EnablePDEV failed.
- The GPD has 132 features; our selections held 128 and the rest read
  past them (a crash in DrvGetDriverSetting). Up to 512 now.
- Commands are built of value macros from Microsoft's PCL XL and PJL
  include files (*Cmd: =ubyte_array =sLetterPaper =attr_ubyte =MediaSize
  =BeginPage): =NAME tokens inside a command were not expanded; a %
  written in hex (<2525>) was not one %; and several entries on one line
  ({ *Order: ... *Cmd: ... }) were read as one.
- A plug-in that hooks the blits is handed the page through them (Unidrv's
  DrvCopyBits and DrvBitBlt, the surface associated with those hooks), and
  for a vector printer language (*Personality PCLXL or HPGL2) Unidrv sends
  no raster of its own and does not band the page; what the plug-in passes
  back lands on the page bitmap.
- A plug-in whose EnablePDEV fails fails the device, as on Windows, rather
  than printing without it.
- A PCL XL GPD without such a plug-in gets each band as one raster block
  (CmdBeginRaster, CmdSendBlockData, CmdEndRaster), rows padded to DWORDs.

HP's Universal Printing PCL 6 driver now prints valid PCL XL that renders
as the page.

Test: test/unidrvxl-gate.sh with test/unidrvxl-plugin.c (mutants
SG_MUTANT_CMDMACRO, HEXPERCENT, FEATURES, ONELINE, PLUGINDRAW,
BLOCKRASTER, DMDRIVEROBJ); test/printdrv-gate.sh still passes.
